From: WPE4YDPv2 maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] WebRTC: do not suspend live MediaStream playback offscreen

MediaStream viewport updates are intentionally ignored by
setViewportVisibility(), but managePlayerSuspend() still applies the generic
muted offscreen-video policy. A newly created remote video player therefore
keeps the default not-visible value, saves its PLAYING request for a resume
that never arrives, and leaves its live appsrc in PAUSED/NO_PREROLL while
decoded frames accumulate.

MediaStream tracks are already controlled by their producers and must keep
flowing for WebRTC first-frame and DataChannel state machines. Exclude only
MediaStream players from this visibility power optimization, including the
initial pipeline setup before the source element has been attached. Regular
URL, Blob and MediaSource video retains the existing suspension behavior.

diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
@@ -3620,7 +3620,8 @@ void MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer::createGSTPlayBin(const URL& url)
             g_object_set(m_pipeline.get(), "audio-filter", scale, nullptr);
     }
 
-    managePlayerSuspend();
+    if (!isMediaStream)
+        managePlayerSuspend();
 #if ENABLE(MEDIA_TELEMETRY)
     MediaTelemetryReport::singleton().reportDrmInfo(getDrm());
     MediaTelemetryReport::singleton().reportPlaybackState(MediaTelemetryReport::AVPipelineState::Create);
@@ -4176,7 +4176,7 @@ void MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer::managePlayerSuspend()
     // this using an environment variable, set from the webkitpy glib port sub-classes.
     auto allowPlaybackOfInvisibleVideos = CStringView::unsafeFromUTF8(g_getenv("WEBKIT_GST_ALLOW_PLAYBACK_OF_INVISIBLE_VIDEOS"));
     bool muted = isMuted();
-    bool shouldBeSuspended = (player && player->isVideoPlayer()) && muted && !m_isVisibleInViewport && allowPlaybackOfInvisibleVideos != "1"_s;
+    bool shouldBeSuspended = !isMediaStreamPlayer() && (player && player->isVideoPlayer()) && muted && !m_isVisibleInViewport && allowPlaybackOfInvisibleVideos != "1"_s;
     GST_INFO_OBJECT(m_pipeline.get(), "%s %s player %svisible in viewport", muted ? "Muted" : "Un-muted", (player && player->isVideoPlayer()) ? "video" : "audio", m_isVisibleInViewport ? "" : "not ");
 
     if (shouldBeSuspended && !isSuspended()) {
